.TH PP 1 "August 2026" "ProtoPeek 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pp \- short executable name for ProtoPeek
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pp
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ target ]
.br
.B pp download
.RI [ --output " NAME" ]
.RI [ --sha256 " 64_HEX" ]
.I URL
.br
.B pp migrate-gobarry
.RI [ --apply ]
.RI [ --preferences= bool ]
.RI [ --session= bool ]
.br
.B pp migrate-gobarry
.BI --rollback " RECEIPT_ID"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pp
is an identical executable entrypoint for
.BR protopeek .
Use the canonical name if another installed program already owns
.BR pp .
.SH DOWNLOADER COMMAND
ProtoPeek v0.5.0 ships
.BR "pp download" .
It accepts exactly one absolute HTTP(S) URL without user information, an
optional safe output filename with no directory components, and an optional
exact 64-hexadecimal-character SHA-256 digest. It uses a configured or system
.BR aria2c ;
aria2 is not bundled.
.PP
Homebrew and Scoop install v0.5.0 and declare aria2 as an external package
dependency, so those package-manager installs provide the Downloader and
migration commands without bundling aria2 into ProtoPeek.
.PP
The one-shot command owns its local engine session instead of attaching to an
already-running ProtoPeek process. It writes progress to standard error and the
completed path to standard output. An interrupt returns status 130 and
preserves partial data plus the aria2 session. See
.BR protopeek (1)
for the complete lifecycle and flag constraints.
.SH GOBARRYGO MIGRATION COMMAND
ProtoPeek v0.5.0 also ships
.BR "pp migrate-gobarry" .
With no mutation flag it only previews the bounded, known GoBarryGo local
profile. Use
.B --apply
to copy compatible state,
.B --preferences=false
for a session-only import, or
.B --session=false
for a preferences-only import. Source files remain unchanged and imported
session jobs remain paused.
.PP
Each successful import creates private state and a guarded receipt. Use
.BI "pp migrate-gobarry --rollback " RECEIPT_ID
only while current ProtoPeek transfer state still matches that receipt;
otherwise rollback refuses to overwrite newer work. Stop both GoBarryGo and
the ProtoPeek Downloader before the final preview/import, and stop the
Downloader before rollback. See
.BR protopeek (1)
for the full safety contract.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR protopeek (1)
